<section class="sc-pl-section"><div class="sc-pl-wrap"><h2>Common reasons customers request this service</h2><div class="sc-pl-grid"><div class="sc-pl-card"><h3>Leaks and water damage</h3><p>Dripping fixtures, wet cabinets, ceiling stains, slab moisture, running meters, mold concerns, and unexplained water bills require prompt investigation.</p></div><div class="sc-pl-card"><h3>Drain and sewer symptoms</h3><p>Slow drains, recurring backups, gurgling, sewer odors, multiple affected fixtures, and yard wet spots can indicate a larger drainage problem.</p></div><div class="sc-pl-card"><h3>Equipment and fixture failures</h3><p>No hot water, leaking water heaters, malfunctioning toilets, low pressure, broken valves, and outdated fixtures often require repair or replacement.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="sc-pl-section"><div class="sc-pl-wrap"><h2>Process</h2><div class="sc-pl-grid"><div class="sc-pl-card"><h3>1. Intake</h3><p>Document symptoms, urgency, location, and access.</p></div><div class="sc-pl-card"><h3>2. Diagnose</h3><p>Inspect, test, isolate, and confirm the likely cause before authorizing major work.</p></div><div class="sc-pl-card"><h3>3. Scope</h3><p>Define repair, replacement, restoration, exclusions, permits, and schedule.</p></div><div class="sc-pl-card"><h3>4. Verify</h3><p>Test operation, check for leaks, document results, and provide maintenance guidance.</p></div></div></div></section>
